<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Canute Guild</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as St Canute's Guild</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Canute <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guild">Guild</a> was a guild of craftsmen in Reval (Tallinn), named after the Danish saint Canute and dominated by German master artisans. With the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/olaf-guild">Olaf Guild</a> it represented the town's craftsmen, below the Great Guild of merchants that controlled the town council. Its 19th-century guild hall on Pikk Street still stands.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/canute-guild.jpg" alt="Canute Guild" width="320" height="480" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Vamps · CC BY-SA 3.0 ee · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Tallinna_Kanuti_gildi_hoone,_1863_(2).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
